course: dictionary
lesson: 4993
title: Indirect: not straight, not plain
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Indirect means not straight, not plain, or not the main way. A direct route goes straight to the place, while an indirect route winds round, so you get there the long way.
explain: Words can be indirect too. A direct request asks plainly, but an indirect one goes round the point to be polite. «An indirect request is a polite way of asking someone to do something, like "Would you mind closing the window?"» The speaker asks a question, but really wants the window shut.
explain: In grammar, indirect speech reports what someone said without their exact words. «Indirect (reported) speech tells what someone said without their exact words and has no inverted commas: She said that she was tired.»
fact: Indirect means not direct: not straight, not plain, or not the main way.
fact: «Indirect» means not going straight, as in an indirect route.
fact: «Indirect» means not said openly or plainly, as in an indirect answer.
fact: «Indirect» can mean a side result, as in an indirect cause.
fact: In grammar, an indirect object receives the thing given: in «She gave me a book», me is the indirect object.
exercise: What does indirect mean in «an indirect route»? | Next to the sea | Very fast | *Not going straight | Painted green
exercise: In «Would you mind closing the window?», what kind of request is it? | A fact about glass | *A polite, indirect request | A test of spelling | A rude order shouted loudly
exercise: Which sentence is indirect speech? | Tired is a word for sleepy. | *She said that she was tired. | "Tired!" shouted Sam. | "I am tired," she said.
test: In «She gave me a book», what is me? | The name of the book | *The indirect object, who receives the book | A verb meaning to give | An adjective for the book
test: Dad says, "Maybe the bin needs emptying," when he means you must do it. What does indirect mean here? | *Not said openly, but hinted at | Going straight to the point | Said openly and plainly | Happening first
exam: What does indirect mean in the phrase «indirect sunlight»? | Very hot and bright | Coming straight from the sun | Only at night | *Not coming straight, but reaching you another way
